# Motion retunes

When the user asks to improve animation, edit **config first**, not the Three.js/GSAP engine.

## Files

| Concern | Edit |
|---|---|
| Hero A/B/C options (rise / assemble) | `src/lib/heroLogoMotion.js` — preview `?hero=A\|B\|C` |
| Assemble order helpers | `src/lib/heroAssemble.js` |
| Hero GSAP timeline structure | `src/lib/heroLogoTimeline.js` |
| Section reveal timing | `src/lib/revealMotion.js` |
| Reveal action (ScrollTrigger) | `src/lib/reveal.js` |

## Rules

- Prefer GSAP ease strings (`power2.out`, `power3.out`, `sine.inOut`). Avoid `expo.out` for long vertical rises.
- Keep **one** Y-spin (`rotateY: -Math.PI * 2 → 0`) unless asked for more.
- World-Y slide must start below the frustum (`rise.fromYFactor ≥ 1.2`).
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (jump to rest / show final state).
- Timeline labels: `blank` → `rise` → `fill` → `settle` → `idle`.
- Do not reintroduce CSS transitions that fight GSAP inline styles on reveal targets.
